\"nodes_with_full\":3,\"restarted\":[0,1],\"servers_after\":[3,3,3]}\nCA_EVENT {\"any_leader\":true,\"event\":\"after_losing_configured_voter_restore_off\",\"leader_index\":1,\"live_voters\":2,\"log_last_index\":\"13,13\",\"mode\":\"restore_off\",\"nodes_with_full\":2,\"servers_after\":[3,3]}\n--- PASS: TestAssurance_PartialRestartLosesLiveQuorum (6.42s)\nPASS\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='update.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nd['gaps']=[\n {\\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"9c549c026d7341f2b1e328826eac6dc3-question-0\\\",\n  \\\"question\\\":\\\"The stale base turns a single requested AddVoter into the removal of a second voter in the same log entry ({A,B,C} -> {A,B,E}), i.e. a two-server change that Raft's single-server-change discipline forbids. Can running nodes then hold disjoint majorities (old {A,B,C} majority without E versus new {A,B,E} majority without C) and elect two leaders in different terms for the same log?\\\",\n  \\\"experiment_id\\\":None}\n]\nd['experiment']={\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"9c549c026d7341f2b1e328826eac6dc3-question-0\\\",\n \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_partial_restart_test.go\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"newraft_scan\\\",\\\"restore_committed\\\",\\\"follower_abort\\\",\\\"heartbeat_timeout_election\\\",\\\"vote_config_checks\\\",\\\"prevote_config_checks\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Three-voter in-memory cluster {A,B,C} bootstrapped on A, converged, ten commands committed, no snapshot. Only voters A and B are restarted (case restore_on with RestoreCommittedLogs=true, control restore_off with it false) while C keeps running; the restarted voters' fresh transports are wired to each other and to C's live transport in both directions. The probe first observes which node leads (C, the only one still holding the configuration, is expected to win with votes from the configuration-less restarted voters), then stops that configured voter and observes whether the two remaining live voters - a quorum of three, each holding every committed entry (log last index 13 on both) - can elect a leader within six seconds at 50ms timeouts.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"Restarting two voters while one keeps running is the ordinary rolling/cold restart an operator may perform; all three stores already contain the bootstrapped configuration entry and every committed entry.\\\",\\\"The decision to stop the configured voter afterwards is a normal availability event (the node is gracefully shut down), not a fault injection: two of three voters remain alive and up to date.\\\",\\\"A quorum of two live voters with complete logs is entitled to elect a leader in this cluster, which is exactly what the control case measures.\\\"],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"No partitions, no disk faults, no message loss, no injected delays.\\\",\\\"The election fan-out to the stopped node is not traced; the observation is the absence of any leader among the live voters.\\\"],\n  \\\"parameters\\\":{\\\"protocol_version\\\":3,\\\"peers\\\":3,\\\"restarted\\\":2,\\\"heartbeat_timeout_ms\\\":50,\\\"election_timeout_ms\\\":50,\\\"opportunity_seconds\\\":6}},\n \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"Real bootstrap and replication to all three voters, real election, real applies, graceful shutdown of A and B only, restart of A and B on the same stores with fresh transports rewired to the live peer, real graceful shutdown of the remaining configured voter. All configuration and log state comes from those operations; the control repeats the identical procedure with RestoreCommittedLogs=false.\\\",\n \\\"prerequisites\\\":[\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_partial_on\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"partial_restart_restore_on\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"restore_on\\\"}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_partial_off\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"partial_restart_restore_off\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"restore_off\\\"}]}\n ],\n \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"after_losing_configured_voter_restore_on\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_partial_on\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"any_leader\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"A live quorum of two up-to-date voters must be able to elect a leader after the third voter stops, even when the other two were restarted with RestoreCommittedLogs enabled.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"after_losing_configured_voter_restore_off\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_partial_off\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"any_leader\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Control: the identical restart and shutdown without RestoreCommittedLogs leaves the two live voters able to elect a leader.\\\"}\n ]\n}\ni=d['interpretations'][0]\ni['executions']={'430d7ba602ed4666bdfe63a96c71e2fc':[1],'d2d1cb0951b74a2984ec525710e4c740':[1,3],'edfd3c204c654542a8bdb4263f290d4d':[1],'4f4a771f03b649c2a5703b0ff279ff3a':[1]}\ni['counterevidence']=i['counterevidence']+[\n \\\"The cluster-wide receipt 4f4a771f03b649c2a5703b0ff279ff3a scores the control comparison holds (index 3, nodes_with_full_config=3) and the failing case violated (index 1, nodes_with_full_config=0), so the empty configuration after a simultaneous restart is specific to the replayed committed prefix.\\\"]\ni['limitations']=[\n \\\"All executions are in-process in-memory clusters at protocol version 3 with 50ms heartbeat/election timeouts and a single committed configuration change; joint-consensus or multi-step changes are not exercised.\\\",\n \\\"The multi-node progress consequence (a live quorum of up-to-date voters unable to elect after the configured voter stops) is the subject of the partial-restart experiment requested in this update; the authority consequence that configuration-less nodes still grant votes is observed indirectly there (the configured voter wins their votes) and read from source (raft.go 1663-1672, 1780-1784).\\\",\n \\\"The finding is specific to RestoreCommittedLogs=true with a CommitTrackingLogStore; with the flag disabled the same durable state recovers normally in every receipt.\\\"]\ni['rationale']=i['rationale'].replace(\\\"(3) edfd3c204c654542a8bdb4263f290d4d index 1: the isolated control with RestoreCommittedLogs=false scores holds (servers_after=1 against the same bootstrapped voter), so the replayed committed prefix, not restart itself, is the cause.\\\",\n \\\"(3) edfd3c204c654542a8bdb4263f290d4d index 1: the isolated control with RestoreCommittedLogs=false scores holds (servers_after=1 against the same bootstrapped voter), so the replayed committed prefix, not restart itself, is the cause. (4) 4f4a771f03b649c2a5703b0ff279ff3a index 1: restarting all three voters at once with the flag leaves servers_after=[0,0,0] and nodes_with_full_config=0 with no leader in a six-second opportunity, while the same procedure without the flag scores holds at index 3 (nodes_with_full_config=3, leader elected) - a cluster-wide progress loss, not a single node's lost context.\\\")\njson.dump(d, open(p,'w'), indent=2)\nEOF\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run; /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run . --submission update.json 2>&1 | head -5\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
