voters while one keeps running is the ordinary rolling/cold restart an operator may perform; all three stores already contain the bootstrapped configuration entry and every committed entry.\\\",\\\"The decision to stop the configured voter afterwards is a normal availability event (the node is gracefully shut down), not a fault injection: two of three voters remain alive and up to date.\\\",\\\"A quorum of two live voters with complete logs is entitled to elect a leader in this cluster, which is exactly what the control case measures.\\\"],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"No partitions, no disk faults, no message loss, no injected delays.\\\",\\\"The election fan-out to the stopped node is not traced; the observation is the absence of any leader among the live voters.\\\"],\n  \\\"parameters\\\":{\\\"protocol_version\\\":3,\\\"peers\\\":3,\\\"restarted\\\":2,\\\"heartbeat_timeout_ms\\\":50,\\\"election_timeout_ms\\\":50,\\\"opportunity_seconds\\\":6}},\n \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"Real bootstrap and replication to all three voters, real election, real applies, graceful shutdown of A and B only, restart of A and B on the same stores with fresh transports rewired to the live peer, real graceful shutdown of the remaining configured voter. All configuration and log state comes from those operations; the control repeats the identical procedure with RestoreCommittedLogs=false.\\\",\n \\\"prerequisites\\\":[\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_partial_on\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"partial_restart_restore_on\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"restore_on\\\"}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_partial_off\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"partial_restart_restore_off\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"restore_off\\\"}]}\n ],\n \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"after_losing_configured_voter_restore_on\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_partial_on\\\",\n   \