rackingLogStore; with the flag disabled the same durable state recovers normally in every receipt.\\\"]\ni['rationale']=i['rationale'].replace(\\\"(3) edfd3c204c654542a8bdb4263f290d4d index 1: the isolated control with RestoreCommittedLogs=false scores holds (servers_after=1 against the same bootstrapped voter), so the replayed committed prefix, not restart itself, is the cause.\\\",\n \\\"(3) edfd3c204c654542a8bdb4263f290d4d index 1: the isolated control with RestoreCommittedLogs=false scores holds (servers_after=1 against the same bootstrapped voter), so the replayed committed prefix, not restart itself, is the cause. (4) 4f4a771f03b649c2a5703b0ff279ff3a index 1: restarting all three voters at once with the flag leaves servers_after=[0,0,0] and nodes_with_full_config=0 with no leader in a six-second opportunity, while the same procedure without the flag scores holds at index 3 (nodes_with_full_config=3, leader elected) - a cluster-wide progress loss, not a single node's lost context.\\\")\njson.dump(d, open(p,'w'), indent=2)\nEOF\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run; /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run . --submission update.json 2>&1 | head -5\"","aggregated_output":"{\"valid\": true, \"run_id\": \"af7ab1df563f4f5686eb47935464cf57\", \"elapsed_seconds\": 741.383746321, \"diagnostics\": [], \"meaning\": \"Read-only validation of these bytes and saved state; no acceptance, execution or budget reservation\", \"no_change\": false, \"execution_requested\": true}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"The cluster-scale receipt (4f4a771f03b649c2a5703b0ff279ff3a) scored cleanly: with RestoreCommittedLogs all three voters come back empty and no leader emerges (violated, witness index 1), while the same simultaneous restart without the flag keeps all three configured and re-elects (control holds, index 3). The interpretation now cites four receipts including that one, confirming a cluster-wide rather than single-node loss. I also ran a partial-restart probe: with only two of three voters restarted, the untouched configured voter leads with the configuration-less nodes' votes (servers [0,0,3]), and once that voter stops, the two remaining live, fully up-to-date voters (log index 13 on both) cannot elect a leader in six seconds at 50ms timeouts — while the no-flag control re-elects immediately. That experiment is submitted for a retained receipt, and I registered a new gap asking whether the silently produced two-server change ({A,B,C} -> {A,B,E}) can let running nodes hold disjoint majorities and elect two leaders.\"}"}}
